Relevant columns, their potential use and some typical conditions  

• `event_name`: identify the row that represents a session start – `WHERE event_name = 'session_start'`  
• `event_date`: cohorting and time–window logic – normally converted with `PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d',event_date)`  
• `event_timestamp`: when sub‑day precision is needed (not required here)  
• `user_pseudo_id`: stable anonymous user id that lets us recognise the same user in later weeks  
• `event_params`: sometimes used to qualify the event, but not needed for a plain session‑start analysis  
• `stream_id` / `platform` / device / geo … : can be added for segmentation but are not required for raw retention

Typical basic filter  
```
WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
  AND PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d',event_date) >= DATE '2018-07-02'
```

Below are ten exploratory → analytical queries that gradually build up to the final answer.  
(The project, dataset and tables come straight from the catalogue you provided.)

